5. FORM VALIDATION
================================================================================

Form data should normally be validated before submission.

Example:

const handleSubmit = (e) => {

  e.preventDefault();

  const errors = {};


  if (!formData.email.includes('@')) {
    errors.email = 'Invalid email';
  }


  if (formData.password.length < 8) {
    errors.password =
      'Password must be at least 8 characters';
  }


  if (Object.keys(errors).length > 0) {

    setErrors(errors);
    return;

  }


  console.log('Form is valid, submitting...');

};


Flow:

Submit Form
     |
     v
e.preventDefault()
     |
     v
Validate Data
     |
     v
Any Errors?
   /     \
 Yes      No
  |        |
  v        v
Display   Submit
Errors    Data


