6. CHECKBOX HANDLING
================================================================================

Checkboxes are slightly different from normal text inputs.

Text Input:
-> Uses value

Checkbox:
-> Uses checked


Example:

const [formData, setFormData] = useState({
  agreeToTerms: false
});


const handleChange = (e) => {

  const { name, type, checked, value } = e.target;

  setFormData({
    ...formData,
    [name]: type === 'checkbox' ? checked : value
  });

};


Checkbox:

<label>

  <input
    type="checkbox"
    name="agreeToTerms"
    checked={formData.agreeToTerms}
    onChange={handleChange}
  />

  I agree to the terms

</label>


Key Rule:

Text Input
-> value={state}

Checkbox
-> checked={state}


