9. CONTROLLED VS. UNCONTROLLED COMPONENTS
================================================================================

CONTROLLED COMPONENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

React state controls the value.

Example:

const [name, setName] = useState('');

<input
  value={name}
  onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)}
/>


Benefits:

- State is the single source of truth
- Easy validation
- Easy reset
- Predictable behavior
- Easy real-time feedback
- Values can be changed programmatically


UNCONTROLLED COMPONENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The DOM maintains the input value.

Example:

<input
  defaultValue="initial"
  ref={inputRef}
/>


Uncontrolled inputs can still be useful in some situations, but controlled
components are commonly preferred when you need validation, dynamic UI,
or detailed control over form state.


